@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1

### 1. Create a new ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "Internet connection issue",
  "description": "Unable to connect to the office Wi-Fi since morning.",
  "priority": "high"
}

### 2. Get all tickets (No filters)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets

### 3. Get tickets with filters (Status & Priority)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?status=open&priority=high

### 4. Get tickets with pagination (Page & Limit)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?page=1&limit=5

### 5. Get tickets with all query parameters combined
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?status=open&priority=high&page=1&limit=10&status=banana

### 6. Test sorted by
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?status=open&priority=high&page=1&limit=10&sortedBy=banana

### 7. Test sorted by with DESC order
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?status=open&priority=high&page=1&limit=10&sortedBy=desc&s


### 6. Get a single ticket by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/1

### 7. Test Validation Error - Invalid Priority on Create
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "Test ticket",
  "description": "This is a test description",
  "priority": "invalid-priority"
}

### 8. Test Create with invalid values
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "Test ticket",
  "description": "This is a test description",
  "sama": "masa"
}

### 8. Test Validation Error - Invalid Filter (Limit < 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?limit=0
